First check your installed Falco configuration and service:

```bash
sudo systemctl status falco --no-pager
sudo grep -n -A5 -B2 'json_output\\|file_output' /etc/falco/falco.yaml
```

In `/etc/falco/falco.yaml`, ensure JSON output is enabled and file output points to the path below. Configuration layouts can differ by Falco version; merge these settings into the existing configuration rather than replacing the whole file:

```yaml
json_output: true
file_output:
  enabled: true
  keep_alive: false
  filename: /var/log/falco/events.json
```

Then:

```bash
sudo install -d -m 0750 /var/log/falco
sudo systemctl restart falco
sudo systemctl status falco --no-pager
```

If your Falco package uses a different config path or service name, use the path/service shown by your installation. Verify that the configured output file is being written before proceeding:

```bash
sudo tail -n 5 /var/log/falco/events.json
```

Each event should be one JSON object per line. Do not add a second `file_output` block if one already exists.
